  "artifact_text": "### 1. Observations and Ruled-Out Leads\n- In deployment log CI-2459, DB_HOST in ConfigMap orders-config was updated to orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432.\n- In pod orders-api-7b7dfdc66d-s2556 logs, the application repeatedly reports failure to resolve orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432 with name not known.\n- In namespace demo-apps, the Service list contains orders-db, but no Service named orders-db-primary exists.\n- Ruled out pod crashes because pod status shows zero restarts and the container remains in Running state.\n- Ruled out scheduling or image pull failures because pod events confirm successful scheduling and image pull.\n\n### 2. Root Cause\nDeployment CI-2459 pointed orders-api to nonexistent service orders-db-primary, causing the database check in the readiness probe to return HTTP 503.\n\n### 3. Recommended Action\nThe orders team should revert DB_HOST in ConfigMap orders-config to orders-db.demo-apps.svc:5432 and restart deployment orders-api.",
